From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:37:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 142/143] kk: a workaround MESA_KK_DISABLE_WORKAROUNDS names
 stays disabled on Apple10

kk_parse_environment_options sets the bits the variable names first,
then the OS and GPU family rules, and the Apple10 rule clears bit 2
unconditionally. The A19 Pro is Apple10, so MESA_KK_DISABLE_WORKAROUNDS=2
(or =all) cannot turn workaround 2 off on the phone: every MSL loop
stays `for (uint64_t no_crash = 0; no_crash < UINT64_MAX; ++no_crash)`,
a 64-bit induction variable (two more live registers, an add with
carry and a 64-bit compare an iteration). RDR2's MSL has 3,770 such
loops in 479 files. The workaround is for an M5 compiler hang on three
CTS reconvergence cases under macOS 27 betas (workarounds.rst) and was
never checked on iOS 27.

What the variable names is now also set again after those rules, so
the list the user gives wins. Unset, the bits are exactly as before.
The bits are hashed into the pipeline cache UUID and the disk cache's
driver id (kk_physical_device_init_pipeline_cache, after this parse),
so a run with workaround 2 off does not reuse MSL built with it on.

A/B on the phone: MESA_KK_DISABLE_WORKAROUNDS=2 against unset; watch
for a library build that never returns or fails.

Linear: PLA-541
Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: $PLAYPORT_BUILD/agent-notes/pla541/kk-compiler.md (finding 4,
 WA2 loop counts)
Offered-upstream: no
---
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c
index fb894f3..5687be2 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c
@@ -1228,18 +1228,23 @@ kk_parse_environment_options(struct kk_physical_device *pdev)
       settings->pass_prof = false;
    }
 
+   /* Playport (PLA-541): what MESA_KK_DISABLE_WORKAROUNDS names stays
+    * disabled whatever the OS and GPU family rules below turn back on
+    * (workaround 2 on Apple10, the A19 Pro); unset, nothing changes */
+   uint64_t named = 0;
    const char *list = debug_get_option("MESA_KK_DISABLE_WORKAROUNDS", "");
    const char *all_workarounds = "all";
    const size_t all_len = strlen(all_workarounds);
    for (unsigned n; n = strcspn(list, ","), *list; list += MAX2(1, n)) {
       if (n == all_len && !strncmp(list, all_workarounds, n)) {
-         settings->disabled_workarounds = UINT64_MAX;
+         named = UINT64_MAX;
          break;
       }
 
       int index = atoi(list);
-      settings->disabled_workarounds |= BITFIELD64_BIT(index);
+      named |= BITFIELD64_BIT(index);
    }
+   settings->disabled_workarounds |= named;
 
    /* Workarounds resolved on macOS 27 */
    if (ns_is_os_version_at_least(27, 0, 0) && !KK_DEBUG(OS26_WORKAROUNDS)) {
@@ -1273,6 +1278,7 @@ kk_parse_environment_options(struct kk_physical_device *pdev)
    if (pdev->info.gpu_apple_family < 9) {
       settings->disabled_workarounds |= BITFIELD64_BIT(18);
    }
+   settings->disabled_workarounds |= named;
 }
 
 VkResult
